Package: georefapp
Type: Package
Title: Batch Georeferencing of Textual Localities
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
      person("Gilles", "Dauby", , "gilles.dauby@ird.fr", role = c("aut", "cre"),
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9498-413X"))
    )
Description: Shiny application for georeferencing lists of plain-text localities,
    with a focus on Central Africa. Localities are imported as a table and grouped
    into distinct normalised strings, so that each distinct locality is
    georeferenced once and every record sharing it inherits the result. A
    georeference is made by drawing a point, circle, line or polygon on a map;
    the coordinate and its uncertainty are derived from the minimum bounding
    circle of the drawn footprint, following the point-radius method. Every
    decision is written to an append-only log held in a local project file, so
    that the Darwin Core output can be regenerated, audited and revised without
    ever losing an earlier interpretation.
